- system_vocabulary
-  sept
' Compatibility facade for the shared system slot vocabulary.
+  bond
  '  The slot vocabulary, one member per well-known key.
  +  content
    '  The primary item at this name.
    '
    '  This is the default target of most overlays that act on a pail.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/content
  +  src
    '  Textual source.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/src
  +  lede
    '  A short title for this name.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/lede
  +  help
    '  A longer description of what the name is/does.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/help
  +  mold
    '  Canonical type description of a published definition.
    '
    '  The descriptor is grounded in the selected system publication.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/mold
  +  limb
    '  List of transition functions that govern the evolution of a path.
    '
    '  A list of paths to records whose /sys/form slot holds a behavior.
    '  The behavior chain: if present, must be a list of paths
    '  to behaviors; if absent, treated as if ~, meaning the path is
    '  unconstrained.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/limb
  +  form
    '  A behavior implementation referenced by a /sys/limb list.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/form
  +  crew
    '  The dependency map: from local slot name to (care, path).
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/crew
  +  author
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/author
  +  unreads
    '  Used to indicate that a path has unreads.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/unreads
  +  req
    '  The request record on a driver-minted node.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/req
  +  res
    '  The response record a serving behavior writes back.  Presence is
    '  the completion signal — there is no separate done flag.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/res
  +  weft
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/weft
  +  tack
    '  The /x view lens's data dependency: a y-care safe pinning the
    '  subtree the node's weft runs against.
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/tack
  +  face
    '  The datum face binding: a hunt whose care is BOTH the ctor's
    '  input care and the claim reach over this record's subtree
    '  (.x the node alone, .y plus its direct kids, .z the whole
    '  subtree), and whose path names the component ctor node the
    '  page renders through ("."-headed rebases at mount, so it is
    '  absolute post-mount — unlike a face kook's ['hunt] claim,
    '  whose path stays mount-root-relative).
    ^  path
    system_vocabulary/face
  +  lash
    ^ path
    system_vocabulary/lash
  +  op
    ^ path
    system_vocabulary/op
  +  about
    ^ path
    system_vocabulary/about
  +  from
    ^ path
    system_vocabulary/from
  +  now
    ^ path
    system_vocabulary/now
  + epoch
    ' A counter used for the purposes of triggering actions or sync
    system_vocabulary/epoch
  + pending
    ' Something waiting
    system_vocabulary/pending
